==Trivia==
* Gas has been nominated to be added to the game since [[Update 13]].
* Gas is the most expensive [[Elemental]] fruit in the game as of [[Update 24]]
* Gas is the first [[Elemental]] fruit to have a [[Mutations|mutation]] in Blox Fruits, being [[Hellfire]].
* Gas' Elemental Immunity SFX is the same as [[Smoke]]'s Elemental Immunity SFX.
* {{Ability|Gas|X}} is locked at the players location, meaning it follows the player for the move's duration. 
* Gas is the first and only [[Elemental]] fruit that has a transformation.
** Gas is also the fourth non-beast type fruit to have a transformation, the others being [[Venom]], [[Rubber]], and [[Diamond]].
* Gas is the second [[Mythical]] fruit that is Elemental, the first one being [[Dough]].
* {{Ability|Gas|F}} has the capability to cancel [[Light]]'s {{Ability|Light|F}} move.
* Gas can infinitely stun [[Terrorshark]]s and other difficult [[bosses]] such as [[Cake Queen]] with its M1s, though a corner is needed for this to work on normal bosses and NPCs.
* Gas is regarded as one of the best fruits for [[Raids]], though the M1 for this fruit will severely slow down a [[Raids|Raid]] if not used correctly.
* It takes 5 minutes and 30 seconds to fill the Gas Meter without doing any damage.
** Using the [[Kitsune Mask]], this can be reduced down to 3 minutes and 12 seconds, making it extremely useful if the user transforms often.
* Gas's transformation lasts for 10 minutes (a full [[Nychthemeron|day cycle]]) if the user did not deal any damage to other enemies/players.
* Gas is one of the three [[Elemental]] fruits to not have an [[Raids|awakening]], along with [[Smoke]] and [[Blizzard]].
* When used {{Ability|Gas|C}} untransformed move against a [[Sea Beast]], they heat seek to the bottom of it, indicating that right below the water in the area below its chin is its main hitbox, explaining why they cannot be hit when they are about to dive.
* Gas is the only [[Elemental]] fruit to have a [[Power Meter]]. The Gas meter is equivalent to [[Kitsune]]'s Tail meter in terms of how long it takes to fill up, which is about 3 normal fury meters. 
* Gas is incredibly fast in its transformation, capable of even outrunning a Transformed [[Kitsune]] if [[Dashing|dash]]<nowiki/>[[Dashing|ing]].

